@Article(time: 2) {
    @Intro(title: "Introduction to Data Model Creation") {
        Dive into Chapter 1 of the SymbolPicker project, learning how to create robust data models to support a dynamic user interface and ensure smooth integration.
        @Image(source: DDM-Banner, alt: "SwiftData file icon.")  
    }
    
    ## Chapter Purpose
    Chapter 1 introduces the SymbolPicker framework, guiding you through building essential data models for a dynamic SF Symbol picker UI. The focus is on creating a SwiftData model to manage SF Symbols effectively.

    ## What You Will Learn
    In Chapter 1, you’ll discover how to set up a multiplatform Xcode project, integrate the SymbolPicker package using Swift Package Manager, and design a SwiftData model for SF Symbols. By the end, you’ll have a strong data foundation for UI development.

    ## Expanding Your App in Future Chapters
    In subsequent chapters, you’ll enhance these data models to build a dynamic List UI with search functionality and optimize for multiplatform support across iOS, iPadOS, macOS, and visionOS. You’ll also explore advanced configurations to transform your app into a fully functional To-Do App.
}
